      "text": "To find the product of the roots of the polynomial equation \\(3x^3 - x^2 - 20x + 27 = 0\\), we can use Vieta's formulas. For a cubic equation of the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0\\), the product of the roots is given by \\(-\\frac{d}{a}\\).\n\nIn our equation \\(3x^3 - x^2 - 20x + 27 = 0\\), the coefficients are \\(a = 3\\), \\(b = -1\\), \\(c = -20\\), and \\(d = 27\\). According to Vieta's formulas, the product of the roots is:\n\n\\[\n-\\frac{d}{a} = -\\frac{27}{3} = -9\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this using Python code.\n```python\n# Coefficients of the polynomial 3x^3 - x^2 - 20x + 27 = 0\na = 3\nd = 27\n\n# Product of the roots using Vieta's formula\nproduct_of_roots = -d / a\nprint(product_of_roots)\n```\n```output\n-9.0\n```\nThe product of the roots of the equation \\(3x^3 - x^2 - 20x + 27 = 0\\) is \\(\\boxed{-9}\\).",
