    "text": "To find the product of the roots of the polynomial equation \\(3x^3 - x^2 - 20x + 27 = 0\\), we can use Vieta's formulas. Vieta's formulas relate the coefficients of a polynomial to sums and products of its roots.\n\nFor a cubic polynomial of the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0\\), Vieta's formulas tell us that:\n1. The sum of the roots \\(r_1 + r_2 + r_3 = -\\frac{b}{a}\\).\n2. The sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time \\(r_1r_2 + r_2r_3 + r_3r_1 = \\frac{c}{a}\\).\n3. The product of the roots \\(r_1r_2r_3 = -\\frac{d}{a}\\).\n\nIn our equation \\(3x^3 - x^2 - 20x + 27 = 0\\), the coefficients are \\(a = 3\\), \\(b = -1\\), \\(c = -20\\), and \\(d = 27\\).\n\nUsing Vieta's formulas, the product of the roots is given by:\n\\[r_1r_2r_3 = -\\frac{d}{a} = -\\frac{27}{3} = -9.\\]\n\nLet's confirm this using Python code.\n```python\n# Coefficients of the polynomial 3x^3 - x^2 - 20x + 27 = 0\na = 3\nd = 27\n\n# Using Vieta's formula to find the product of the roots\nproduct_of_roots = -d / a\nprint(product_of_roots)\n```\n```output\n-9.0\n```\nThe product of the roots of the equation \\(3x^3 - x^2 - 20x + 27 = 0\\) is \\(\\boxed{-9}\\).",
